{% doc %}
  The video overlay for `sections/testimonials-showcase.liquid`.

  ## One modal for the whole section

  Twelve reviews is not twelve dialogs. Each card carries a `<template>` with
  its own poster, its own play control and its own media, and
  `assets/testimonial-showcase.js` clones the one that was pressed into the
  stage below. The chrome — the ring, the close button, the focus trap, the
  scroll lock — is written once and reused.

  That also makes the lanes' clones harmless. A lane duplicates its cards to
  loop seamlessly, and a modal per card would mean four copies of the same
  dialog id in the document.

  ## The stage is empty until it is asked for

  Nothing is rendered inside it here. Opening fills it; closing empties it, and
  emptying it is what stops playback — `pause()` reaches a hosted video and
  does nothing whatsoever to a YouTube iframe, which would otherwise carry on
  behind a closed overlay with no way to reach it.

  ## Why `<modal-dialog>` rather than a div

  The same reason every other overlay in the theme uses it: the browser owns the
  top layer, the backdrop, the inertness of the page behind and the Escape key.
  What this snippet adds is a shape — a ring around a 16:9 stage — and a close
  button that sits outside the frame rather than over the footage.

  @param {string} id - Unique per section. The section passes `showcase-video-{{ section.id }}`.
  @param {object} settings - The section's settings object.

  @example
    {% render 'showcase-video-modal', id: modal_id, settings: section.settings %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = settings

  assign ring_width = s.modal_ring_width | default: 14 | plus: 0
  assign radius = s.modal_radius | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign max_width = s.modal_width | default: 880 | plus: 0

  comment
    The ring is a translucent white by default rather than a colour picked from
    the scheme: it sits over whatever the page happens to be behind the
    backdrop, and a scheme colour there is a rectangle that changes meaning
    every time the modal opens over a different section.
  endcomment
  assign ring_paint = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28)'
  if s.modal_ring_color != blank
    assign ring_alpha = s.modal_ring_opacity | default: 28 | plus: 0
    assign ring_alpha = ring_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign ring_paint = s.modal_ring_color | color_modify: 'alpha', ring_alpha
  endif

  assign backdrop_blur = s.modal_backdrop_blur | default: 8 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the shape of the stage ----

    Two forms of the same number. `aspect-ratio` takes the pair and gives the
    stage its shape; the decimal is what the width has to be multiplied *back*
    by to work out how wide a panel of a given height can be, and `calc()`
    cannot divide by a `16 / 9`.

    It exists because a testimonial is as often filmed on a phone as on a
    camera, and a portrait video in a 16:9 stage is two black bars with a face
    between them.
  endcomment
  assign modal_ratio = s.modal_ratio | default: '16-9'

  case modal_ratio
    when '9-16'
      assign ratio_pair = '9 / 16'
      assign ratio_value = 0.5625
    when '4-5'
      assign ratio_pair = '4 / 5'
      assign ratio_value = 0.8
    when '1-1'
      assign ratio_pair = '1 / 1'
      assign ratio_value = 1
    when '4-3'
      assign ratio_pair = '4 / 3'
      assign ratio_value = 1.3333
    else
      assign ratio_pair = '16 / 9'
      assign ratio_value = 1.7778
  endcase

  assign entrance = s.modal_animation | default: 'zoom-out'
  assign entrance_duration = s.modal_animation_duration | default: 360 | plus: 0

  assign modal_label = 'sections.testimonials_showcase.modal_label' | t

  comment
    ---- the play badge ----

    Its settings live on the section and are written onto *this* element rather
    than onto the section root, because the modal is a sibling of the section
    and custom properties inherit down a tree rather than across one. The badge
    is markup cloned in from a card, so the only ancestor it is guaranteed to
    have is this one.
  endcomment
  assign badge_size = s.badge_size | default: 112 | plus: 0
  assign badge_spin = s.badge_spin | default: 12 | plus: 0
-%}

{%- capture modal_style -%}
  --sv-modal-ring: {{ ring_width }}px;
  --sv-modal-ring-color: {{ ring_paint }};
  --sv-modal-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --sv-modal-width: {{ max_width }}px;
  --sv-modal-ratio: {{ ratio_pair }};
  --sv-modal-ratio-value: {{ ratio_value }};
  --sv-modal-backdrop-blur: {{ backdrop_blur }}px;
  --sv-badge-size: {{ badge_size }}px;
  --sv-badge-spin: {{ badge_spin }}s;
  {%- if s.modal_backdrop_color != blank -%}
    --sv-modal-backdrop: {{ s.modal_backdrop_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.badge_background != blank -%}
    --sv-badge-background: {{ s.badge_background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.badge_text_color != blank -%}
    --sv-badge-text: {{ s.badge_text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<modal-dialog
  id="{{ id }}"
  class="modal showcase-modal"
  data-overlay-type="video"
  data-animation="{{ entrance }}"
  data-animation-duration="{{ entrance_duration }}"
  style="{{ modal_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  <dialog class="modal__dialog showcase-modal__dialog" data-ref="dialog" aria-label="{{ modal_label | escape }}">
    <div class="modal__panel showcase-modal__panel" data-ref="panel">
      {%- comment -%}
        Outside the ring, at the corner, which is where the design puts it and
        where it cannot be mistaken for part of the footage. It is the first
        thing in the panel so it is also the first thing focus lands on.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="showcase-modal__close"
        data-overlay-close
        aria-label="{{ 'general.actions.close' | t }}"
      >
        {% render 'icon', icon: 'close', size: 16 %}
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        Filled by `assets/testimonial-showcase.js` with a clone of the pressed
        card's template, and emptied again on close. Deliberately not
        `aria-live`: the customer pressed play, so the change is one they asked
        for and announcing it is noise.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="showcase-modal__stage" data-showcase-stage></div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</modal-dialog>
